# Lantage — copy to .env.local and fill in what you have, then restart `npm run dev`.
#
# Nothing here is required to start the app. Each capability that is missing is
# reported in the UI with the exact variable to set, and the modules that don't
# need it keep working. There is no demo mode and no sample data — if a key is
# absent, that section of the result is empty and says why.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VISION — the one key that matters most
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unlocks LOCATE, INTERIOR and VEHICLE. Resolution order is Anthropic, then
# OpenAI, then Gemini — set whichever you have.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Model and reasoning effort for the OpenAI path. The defaults were measured, not
# assumed — see the header of src/lib/live/vision/openai.ts and re-run
# `node scripts/bench-locate.ts` before changing them. Effort is the single
# largest latency term: raising it roughly doubles the wall clock and buys
# nothing on a schema-constrained extraction of what is visible in a frame.
# LANTAGE_OPENAI_VLM_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# LANTAGE_OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Works with NO keys at all
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTHENTIC — C2PA Content Credentials, EXIF/XMP, JPEG quantization forensics.
#   Entirely offline. No key, ever.
# FACE — local ONNX models (YuNet detect + SFace recognise), weights MIT and
#   Apache-2.0, downloaded once to .lantage-models/. No key, no upload of
#   biometrics anywhere. Strictly a 1:1 compare between two images you supply.
# VEHICLE validation — NHTSA vPIC is free and needs no key. It is what stops the
#   vision model inventing a make or model that doesn't exist.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — each adds one capability
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Reverse image search: "has this photo been published anywhere?"
# This is the legitimate route to identifying a specific building — if the
# interior was ever on a listing or rental page, that page names the address.
# Caveat worth knowing: these find copies of YOUR image, not other photos of the
# same room. An original frame nobody ever published will return nothing.
# TINEYE_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_VISION_API_KEY=

# Statistical AI-generation detection, layered after the deterministic checks.
# Plan around ~82% on in-the-wild media, not the 98% vendors advertise.
# HIVE_API_KEY=

# Geocoding, to turn a region name into coordinates. Self-host only — the public
# Nominatim instance forbids systematic queries.
# NOMINATIM_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Dark basemap. Without it the map falls back to a keyless OpenFreeMap style.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PMTILES_URL=

# Live Street View in the side-by-side verification panel. Needs the Maps
# JavaScript API enabled on the key and a browser-side referrer restriction —
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means it ships to the client, so restrict it by HTTP referrer.
# Without it the panel renders an empty placeholder naming this variable; it
# never substitutes a stand-in panorama. Rendering Street View live through the
# official embed is licensed; storing or caching the pixels is not, so nothing
# is persisted beyond pano IDs and coordinates.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Set to `true` ONLY if the Geocoding API is also enabled on the key above. It is
# billed separately, so its presence cannot be inferred from the key. Unset means
# "currently viewing" shows coordinates and no address — never a guessed one.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_GEOCODING_ENABLED=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production path only — NOT needed for local testing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The authenticated /api/search pipeline (audit log, org scoping, Mapillary
# retrieval for street-level precision). The local /api/analyze path needs none
# of it. Never point these at a database holding Criminal Justice Information —
# see docs/MASTER_PLAN.md §7.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# MODAL_EMBED_URL=
# MODAL_EMBED_TOKEN=
# MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Street matching with NO cloud account — docs/HARVEST.md §14
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same street path as above, backed by the harvest SQLite file and a local
# CPU/MPS EigenPlaces server instead of Supabase + Modal. Only used when the
# Supabase vars above are unset — Postgres always wins, because it is the shared
# index and a laptop file silently shadowing it would make two operators
# disagree about what is covered. With neither set, nothing is claimed at all.
#
#   services/inference/.venv/bin/python services/inference/local_server.py
#   python3 services/harvest/embed_index.py --db data/harvest/greenwich.sqlite --target sqlite
#
# LANTAGE_LOCAL_INDEX=data/harvest/greenwich.sqlite
# Optional. Implied as http://localhost:8000 when LANTAGE_LOCAL_INDEX is set;
# set it explicitly if port 8000 is taken.
# LANTAGE_LOCAL_EMBED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8010
